      "evidence": "scripts/select_checks.py (candidate.diff ~4578-4602): with `--execute` and no `--base`, surface_explorer_drift prints an error and returns 2. main() then sets that as the exit code if the template selector succeeded. The same applies to any non-zero exit of `build_explorer.py drift --base`, for example an unresolvable merge base. Drift itself never fails, but drift reporting can fail the whole selected-checks run. This is a tool error, not drift, and the wrapper docstring says so. It is still stricter than 'no check fails because of it'.",
